  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "15",
  "quote": "A provision in a tenancy agreement providing that all or part of the remaining rent for a term or period of a tenancy or a specific sum becomes due upon a default of the tenant in paying rent due or in carrying out an obligation is void.",
  "reason": "Section 15 of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 explicitly prohibits acceleration clauses in tenancy agreements. Therefore, a clause making the remaining rent for the term immediately due upon a missed rent payment is void."
}

